Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: However, as of June 2026, only 41.7% of this target has reportedly been delivered,

1172
01:00:54,100 --> 01:00:56,320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: with only two years remaining before the target date.

1173
01:00:56,740 --> 01:00:57,320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: How common?

1174
01:00:57,360 --> 01:01:03,580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: How confident is DHSUD that it can deliver the remaining 175,000 or so housing units?

1175
01:01:04,340 --> 01:01:07,460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Or what's the new target? Have we adjusted our target?

1176
01:01:08,380 --> 01:01:10,880
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Number one, Mr. Chairman, the target is still the same.

1177
01:01:11,640 --> 01:01:16,380
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Now, we are confident that we will hit that, we will be able to comply with that commitment.

1178
01:01:17,180 --> 01:01:21,160
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: As the numbers will show, yung jump natin from the first three years,

1179
01:01:21,720 --> 01:01:25,580
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: then when we expanded the 4PH by adding modalities,

1180
01:01:26,100 --> 01:01:27,300
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: lumaki talaga yung number.

1181
01:01:27,300 --> 01:01:35,280
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Now, based on that momentum, we are confident that we will still hit the 300,000.

1182
01:01:36,580 --> 01:01:42,700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Okay, I'm hoping also because this will be the acid test for the department.

1183
01:01:43,120 --> 01:01:48,720
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Of course, for this, supposedly the landmark legislation, we are hoping that it will really perform.

1184
01:01:49,880 --> 01:01:53,700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ito rin yung question, kasi nakita ko kanina yung I was asking my staff also.

1185
01:01:53,700 --> 01:01:56,700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, if you would look at the budget of...

1186
01:01:57,300 --> 01:01:59,160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: They should, lalo yung attached agencies.

1187
01:01:59,540 --> 01:02:05,100
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, it's quite low compared to other major departments.

1188
01:02:05,360 --> 01:02:09,640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, sabi ko, syempre, being the author of this, I would want...

1189
01:02:09,640 --> 01:02:12,180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: They should to have bigger budget.

1190
01:02:12,340 --> 01:02:16,980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: But ang problema, with the low obligation and disbursement rate of the program,

1191
01:02:17,300 --> 01:02:24,200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: the question is, why should Congress provide another 1 billion or so in subsidy for 2027

1192
01:02:24,200 --> 01:02:27,200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: while significant prior year subsidy remains?

1193
01:02:27,300 --> 01:02:30,100
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And what specific bottlenecks have been removed?

1194
01:02:30,200 --> 01:02:33,380
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, yun ang ano natin because of the low fiscal space as well.

1195
01:02:33,940 --> 01:02:38,300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Syempre, alam mo naman dito, pag yung unutilized, yung hindi...

1196
01:02:38,900 --> 01:02:46,880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Merong funds that have not been disbursed, especially to the end of the year.

1197
01:02:48,020 --> 01:02:51,200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Talagang kukunin, ano yan, ilalagay sa iba.

1198
01:02:51,200 --> 01:02:53,200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, Sek, ano bang ano natin dito?

1199
01:02:53,720 --> 01:02:56,780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: How can we improve yung ating obligation disbursement rate?

1200
01:02:57,300 --> 01:03:01,100
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So that, at least, if we ask for additional...

1201
01:03:01,100 --> 01:03:03,540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Actually, yung request niya about 2 billion sana, no?

1202
01:03:04,680 --> 01:03:08,740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sabi ko, kung pwede natin bigay, I will, to increase the production.

1203
01:03:09,460 --> 01:03:10,100
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, yun lang.

1204
01:03:10,700 --> 01:03:18,380
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: What specific bottlenecks and prior year subsidy that remains unused, paano natin ito may utilize?

1205
01:03:18,660 --> 01:03:22,820
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: For the unutilized, Mr. Chairman, for the unutilized subsidy budget,

1206
01:03:23,900 --> 01:03:26,640
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: ang naging problema kasi dito during the first three years,

1207
01:03:27,300 --> 01:03:32,120
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: hindi natin na-issue yung IRR for the Horizontal Socialized Housing.

1208
01:03:33,200 --> 01:03:35,420
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: So, nung na-issue po natin ito noong 2025,

1209
01:03:36,580 --> 01:03:43,840
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: nakita na doon po lang nagsimula, gumawa ang karamihan sa mga private sector developers na socialized housing for...

1210
01:03:43,840 --> 01:03:45,240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, there was a considerable delay.

1211
01:03:45,540 --> 01:03:46,680
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: There was a delay in the...

1212
01:03:46,680 --> 01:03:49,100
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Sa pagsimula, waiting for the IRR.

1213
01:03:49,100 --> 01:03:49,780
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: For the IRR.

1214
01:03:49,860 --> 01:03:54,220
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Hindi nila alam magkano yung price ceiling ng, say, 26 square meters, 27, no?

1215
01:03:54,820 --> 01:03:57,100
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Then, if you will note also...

1216
01:03:57,300 --> 01:04:04,040
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: So, for PH kasi, among the modalities, dalawang modalities lang dyan ang nagkakaroon ng interest subsidy.

1217
01:04:04,360 --> 01:04:08,280
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: These are the vertical and horizontal modalities.

1218
01:04:08,720 --> 01:04:14,740
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: So, as I said, ngayon pa lang talaga nagsisimulang matapos yung mga horizontal developments

1219
01:04:14,740 --> 01:04:22,940
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: dahil nag-antay po sila ng IRR sa kabagong price ceiling na ilabas natin noong December 23, 2025.

1220
01:04:23,160 --> 01:04:27,280
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: So, we expect na this year and towards the end of this year,

1221
01:04:27,300 --> 01:04:38,000
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: this year and 2027 po, dadami yung take-out natin ng horizontal housing units na magkakaroon po sila, magkaka-avail po sila noong subsidy.

1222
01:04:38,300 --> 01:04:48,460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, by this time, Sek, siguro yung mga na-delay na projects on will be already ready for occupancy and for disposal and for take-out.

1223
01:04:49,980 --> 01:04:52,820
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: What are the measurable 2027 targets for modality?

1224
01:04:52,820 --> 01:04:57,280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: As you mentioned, vertical, horizontal, enhanced EMP, rental, temporary housing.

1225
01:04:57,300 --> 01:04:59,440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and high-density housing.

1226
01:04:59,980 --> 01:05:01,180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, ano yung pinaka-ano rito?

1227
01:05:01,600 --> 01:05:07,800
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Ang tinitingnan po natin na mataas talaga yung numero is the Community Mortgage Program

1228
01:05:07,800 --> 01:05:11,300
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: and the High-Density Housing Program of SHFC.

1229
01:05:11,420 --> 01:05:14,840
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Ito po yung inihinga natin ng dagdag na budget sana.

1230
01:05:15,380 --> 01:05:19,040
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Requested for about 2 billion for CNP.

1231
01:05:22,380 --> 01:05:27,040
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Tapos, doon sa EDCOM, ito yung EDCOM consortium.

1232
01:05:27,300 --> 01:05:30,520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, ano yung pinaka-ano rito?

1233
01:05:31,420 --> 01:05:38,060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: There are sudden increases in the number of enrollments around NHA resettlement areas, resettlement sites.

1234
01:05:38,060 --> 01:05:45,480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: For example, na-ikavite, na-ikview residences from 40,000 enrollments in school year 2021-2022.

1235
01:05:46,220 --> 01:05:51,660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Decadal enrollments increased to 50,896 in school year 2022-2023.

1236
01:05:52,720 --> 01:05:57,120
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, reflecting 10,794 students, this surge requires,

1237
01:05:57,120 --> 01:06:01,180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: the need for additional 270 classrooms.

1238
01:06:01,940 --> 01:06:08,120
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: In July 2025, the DSHOD and DepEd sign a Memorandum of Understanding for the Coordination of School Lots

1239
01:06:08,120 --> 01:06:11,160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and Facilities within or near housing projects.

1240
01:06:11,300 --> 01:06:15,480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: What progress has been made since DSHOD-DepEd MOE in 2025?

1241
01:06:15,700 --> 01:06:17,520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Do we still coordinate with DSHOD?

1242
01:06:17,640 --> 01:06:19,540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kasi kami concerned with the DepEd?

1243
01:06:20,260 --> 01:06:26,640
NHA General Manager Joeben A. Tai: Mr. Chair, I'd like to inform you that actually we have just about to sign a MOA with DepEd.

1244
01:06:27,120 --> 01:06:27,920
NHA General Manager Joeben A. Tai: Sorry, Angara.

1245
01:06:28,500 --> 01:06:34,260
NHA General Manager Joeben A. Tai: Wherein they will be giving us funds for the construction of almost 50 schools on our resettlement sites.

1246
01:06:35,000 --> 01:06:44,420
NHA General Manager Joeben A. Tai: So, we have this MOA wherein we make sure na these sites of us will be having schools already.

1247
01:06:46,060 --> 01:06:47,300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Okay, so ongoing, ano yan?

1248
01:06:48,440 --> 01:06:49,660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Meron na kayong ongoing.

1249
01:06:49,980 --> 01:06:52,600
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, hopefully we can implement it as DepEd.

1250
01:06:54,000 --> 01:06:56,900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: At ito naman yung sa in-city and near-city housing, actually.

1251
01:06:57,120 --> 01:07:02,140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We just passed, Seto Escudero just finished the committee report.

1252
01:07:03,680 --> 01:07:10,240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: What is DSHOD's policy for prioritizing in-city, near-site, and near-city housing before families are relocated farther away?

1253
01:07:11,340 --> 01:07:12,680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, ito rin pa yung ano natin?

1254
01:07:13,080 --> 01:07:15,280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Do we still encourage in-city and near-city housing?

1255
01:07:15,280 --> 01:07:17,760
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Mr. Chairman, this is the challenge of socialized housing.

1256
01:07:17,900 --> 01:07:19,980
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Yung mga lupa sa mga city, mahal na.

1257
01:07:20,380 --> 01:07:23,220
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: So, we are pushing for rental using LGU land.

1258
01:07:23,500 --> 01:07:24,860
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Kaya, pinaprioritize.

1259
01:07:25,040 --> 01:07:27,100
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Dinagdag din natin as one modality yung rental.

1260
01:07:27,120 --> 01:07:31,160
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Para nga ito magkaroon ng rental housing within the city.

1261
01:07:31,700 --> 01:07:34,120
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Which we are now doing in some LGUs.

1262
01:07:35,900 --> 01:07:42,120
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, I think you mentioned earlier, the best model probably now is the Disciplina Village of Valenzuela.

1263
01:07:43,060 --> 01:07:46,160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Very successful yung kanilang rental housing.

1264
01:07:46,260 --> 01:07:50,800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I think for, especially for NCR, this will really be very applicable.

1265
01:07:51,640 --> 01:07:53,660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kasi karamihan naman dito, really for work.

1266
01:07:53,660 --> 01:07:57,080
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And by retirement, a lot will go.

1267
01:07:57,120 --> 01:07:57,960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Home to their provinces.

1268
01:07:58,360 --> 01:07:59,460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, ilan na po ang ano?

1269
01:07:59,720 --> 01:08:03,980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: How many rental housing projects are ongoing, Secretary?

1270
01:08:04,480 --> 01:08:08,360
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: In terms of number of units, around 5,000 units are under construction now.

1271
01:08:08,880 --> 01:08:10,720
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: In different LGUs.

1272
01:08:10,900 --> 01:08:12,220
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: We will start to...

1273
01:08:12,220 --> 01:08:16,820
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Which LGUs pala are already implementing itong rental housing?

1274
01:08:17,260 --> 01:08:19,400
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Ang isa po dito malaki yung sa Quezon City.

1275
01:08:19,680 --> 01:08:22,220
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Yung Sania property, yung nasunog noong March.

1276
01:08:22,220 --> 01:08:24,900
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Around 2,300 units.

1277
01:08:25,700 --> 01:08:26,820
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Informal settler.

1278
01:08:26,820 --> 01:08:28,080
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: For families po ang naapektuhan.

1279
01:08:28,700 --> 01:08:36,560
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: So, for the meantime, binigyan muna natin ng assistance ng LGU ng Quezon City ng rental subsidy.

1280
01:08:37,160 --> 01:08:37,960
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Yung mga nasunogan.

1281
01:08:38,080 --> 01:08:41,100
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Habang ginagawa ngayon natin yung mga condominium units.

1282
01:08:41,520 --> 01:08:42,560
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Pitong building po ito.

1283
01:08:42,700 --> 01:08:44,720
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Ongoing construction ngayon sa Quezon City.

1284
01:08:45,300 --> 01:08:49,340
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Then meron din po tayong sisimulan sa UP Diliman.

1285
01:08:49,740 --> 01:08:52,240
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Around 1,200 units.

1286
01:08:52,580 --> 01:08:56,360
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Nagkakaroon lang ng konting challenges sa mga informal settlers.

1287
01:08:56,360 --> 01:08:57,800
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Sa pag-relocate sa kanila.

1288
01:08:58,400 --> 01:09:00,700
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: And then we also have in Iloilo.

1289
01:09:01,620 --> 01:09:02,680
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Iloilo City.

1290
01:09:03,340 --> 01:09:03,900
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Cebu.

1291
01:09:04,420 --> 01:09:04,860
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Victoria.

1292
01:09:05,540 --> 01:09:06,940
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: And Los Banos.

1293
01:09:07,060 --> 01:09:13,760
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: So, yun po yung mga pilot rental housing natin na tinatayo ngayon.

1294
01:09:13,860 --> 01:09:20,140
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: And then we are also discussing with other LGUs na sa NCR.

1295
01:09:20,720 --> 01:09:23,580
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Ang challenge dito kasi yung pag-provide nila ng mga lupa.

1296
01:09:24,480 --> 01:09:25,800
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

1297
01:09:25,800 --> 01:09:26,320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

1298
01:09:26,360 --> 01:09:30,900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ito yung inventory natin of Idle Lands.

1299
01:09:32,120 --> 01:09:36,280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: In 2025, they should inventory more than 30,000 hectares.

1300
01:09:36,420 --> 01:09:43,340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: But only about 30% is potentially suitable because of legal and land use restrictions.

1301
01:09:43,840 --> 01:09:47,500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, what current data do we have on the inventory of the Idle Lands?

1302
01:09:48,080 --> 01:09:55,320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And how is the issue planning to address the high cost,

1303
01:09:55,320 --> 01:09:57,200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: limitations, and land ownership challenges?

1304
01:09:57,360 --> 01:09:58,760
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sayang din yung ano natin, inventory.

1305
01:09:59,500 --> 01:10:07,380
DHSUD Senior Undersecretary Henry L. Yap: Mr. Chair, based on the new charter of NHA, na-turnover na po namin yung ginawa naming inventaryo sa NHA.

1306
01:10:07,540 --> 01:10:11,380
DHSUD Senior Undersecretary Henry L. Yap: And they're now studying the data that we have provided them.

1307
01:10:13,680 --> 01:10:14,180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yung ano po,

1308
01:10:15,100 --> 01:10:15,620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sek, no?

1309
01:10:16,780 --> 01:10:19,020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yung 4PH, unang una was

1310
01:10:19,020 --> 01:10:21,300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: vision.

1311
01:10:21,480 --> 01:10:23,740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ang parang naging priority na yun, 4PH horizontal, no?

1312
01:10:23,740 --> 01:10:24,800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yung first three years, tama.

1313
01:10:24,800 --> 01:10:25,580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Vertical.

1314
01:10:25,720 --> 01:10:26,500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I mean, vertical.

1315
01:10:27,560 --> 01:10:27,800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And,

1316
01:10:27,860 --> 01:10:31,800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: ako kasi, I would think that we stick to the

1317
01:10:32,680 --> 01:10:37,200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: decades-long proven formula pag socialized housing.

1318
01:10:37,820 --> 01:10:39,400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: It's really woke up, di ba?

1319
01:10:39,560 --> 01:10:42,840
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Lalo na sa in-city or near-city housing.

1320
01:10:43,680 --> 01:10:46,780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, do you agree that I think,

1321
01:10:47,780 --> 01:10:50,800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: kasi from the time from the bliss housing up to now,

1322
01:10:50,800 --> 01:10:54,680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: yung mga recent socialized housing na medium rise,

1323
01:10:54,800 --> 01:10:57,820
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: our five-story woke up are more successful, I would think.

1324
01:10:58,160 --> 01:11:01,700
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: We agree on that principle, Mr. Chairman.

1325
01:11:01,800 --> 01:11:05,740
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: In fact, we are really pushing for woke up vertical housing.

1326
01:11:05,740 --> 01:11:07,720
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: Kung talagang mapipilitan mag-vertical,

1327
01:11:07,840 --> 01:11:10,180
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: kasi may mga lugar na hindi na talaga pwede yung horizontal.

1328
01:11:11,140 --> 01:11:12,220
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: We are pushing for,

1329
01:11:13,280 --> 01:11:15,860
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: again, looking at the model of Disciplina Village,

1330
01:11:16,000 --> 01:11:18,220
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: talagang nakita natin yung woke up manageable yung

1331
01:11:18,220 --> 01:11:21,900
DHSUD Secretary Jose Ramon P. Aliling: pag-manage ng estate management in the future.

1332
